{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 79","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_79&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Done with her new problems, Wendy takes a break from math. Still without any fresh reading material, she feels a bit antsy. She starts to feel annoyed that Michael's loose papers clutter the family van. Several of them are ripped, and bits of paper litter the floor. Tired of trying to get Michael to clean up after himself, Wendy spends a couple of minutes putting Michael's loose papers in the trash. \"That seems fair to me,\" confirms Hannah encouragingly.\n</p><p>While collecting Michael's scraps, Wendy comes across a corner of a piece of paper with part of a math problem written on it. There is a monic polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, with real coefficients. The first two terms after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c72f3acf1f7744cfe76edaf47e45d62432cf28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab55ad1ee35d18e70b12a31683483720dc608757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}x^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f33fa08d335d388431c35117eba964f603983c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-2}x^{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, but the rest of the polynomial is cut off where Michael's page is ripped. Wendy barely makes out a little of Michael's scribbling, showing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e6f53177beee10f4ce95e3acdb027d4af4aeb49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}=-a_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"10\" />. Wendy deciphers the goal of the problem, which is to find the sum of the squares of the roots of the polynomial. Wendy knows neither the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, nor the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896d56965b17443a55b2b5e55f798adf6465380d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" />, but still she finds a [greatest] lower bound for the answer to the problem. Find the absolute value of that lower bound.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_79&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a>, given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20683ef9727be1ea33baa94bf486fd3a21f3477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\cdots r_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"11\" /> are roots of the polynomial, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/90009a50417ef71e5cb161c5a57bb9f23b9e2bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n r_i = -a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"114\" height=\"48\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27bc142f998451ebc9100f68ed215aef32c92af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2 + r_1r_3 \\cdots r_{n-1}r_n = a_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"222\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFrom the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/90009a50417ef71e5cb161c5a57bb9f23b9e2bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n r_i = -a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"114\" height=\"48\" />, squaring both sides and substituting results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52b6d5eba9e2dfac93394910162df792146363e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{i=1}^n r_i^2 + 2(r_1r_2 + r_1r_3 \\cdots r_{n-1}r_n) &amp;= (a_{n-1})^2 \\\\ \\sum_{i=1}^n r_i^2 + 2a_{n-2} &amp;= (-a_{n-2})^2 \\\\ \\sum_{i=1}^n r_i^2 &amp;= (a_{n-2})^2 - 2a_{n-2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"400\" height=\"163\" />\nTo find the lower bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16965d933a8239a91ec05b0674663b66962804f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n r_i^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"43\" height=\"48\" />, we need to find the lower bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02ae5443d4204efd7937f1959d8e8b18566ba0dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n-2})^2 - 2a_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"19\" />. The minimum of the quadratic is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, so the absolute value of the lower bound of the sum of the squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3547351abf03ab0b6cbda7b0b905b2e4f6220e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_79&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_78\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 78\">Problem 78</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_80\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 80\">Problem 80</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/